From: James Athappilly <jamesatha@meta.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rsa: use OpenSSL ENGINE compatibility stubs

OpenSSL 4 removes ENGINE support and provides compatibility stubs for
legacy callers. Enable them so the host signing tools still link, PEM
signing continues to work, and existing error handling rejects engines
that are unavailable. Older OpenSSL versions ignore this definition.

--- a/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
+++ b/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  */
 
 #define OPENSSL_API_COMPAT 0x10101000L
+#define OPENSSL_ENGINE_STUBS
 
 #include "mkimage.h"
 #include <stdlib.h>
